{"format":"bms-recording-1","id":"exercise","title":"Heart rate during exercise","group":"Breathing and exercise","summary":"Ten minutes of cycling against a high resistance: the heart rate climbs.","description":"An ECG recorded from the chest while a volunteer cycled on an exercise bike against a high resistance for ten minutes. The heart-rate channel shows the rate climbing from about 85 to about 130 beats a minute as the exercise goes on. Zoom in to see that the beats keep their shape while the intervals between them shorten.","look_for":["The heart rate at the start and at the end","The R–R interval at the start and at the end","Which part of the cardiac cycle shortens most as the heart rate rises: systole (QRS to the end of T) or diastole (the end of T to the next QRS)"],"fs":256,"n":150785,"duration":589.004,"file":"exercise.bin","channels":[{"name":"ECG (chest)","short":"ECG","units":"a.u.","kind":"ecg","scale":0.0465278,"offset":-261.663,"range":[-2016.0,1492.0],"about":"two electrodes on the upper chest, one each side of the heart; the database does not give its scale in millivolts"}],"view":{"t0":0,"span":600,"hr":true},"beats":{"channel":0,"t":[0.7773,1.6016,2.4141,3.2344,4.0469,4.8438,5.6172,6.3711,7.1289,7.8633,8.5703,9.2773,10.0,10.6992,11.4102,12.125,12.8281,13.5469,14.2969,15.0859,15.8633,16.6367,17.3867,18.125,18.8398,19.543,20.2539,20.9219,21.6133,22.2852,22.9727,23.6797,24.375,25.1211,25.8672,26.6133,27.3555,28.0977,28.8164,29.5234,30.2188,30.8984,31.5703,32.25,32.9648,33.6914,34.4492,35.2148,35.9688,36.7266,37.4805,38.2227,38.9453,39.6953,40.418,41.1094,41.832,42.5312,43.2227,43.918,44.6094,45.2773,45.9766,46.6328,47.3203,47.9883,48.6602,49.3359,50.0156,50.6875,51.3594,52.0195,52.6719,53.3164,53.9531,54.5859,55.2188,55.832,56.4805,57.1289,57.7617,58.4141,59.0859,59.7344,60.3828,61.0156,61.6328,62.2852,62.8906,63.5352,64.1562,64.7773,65.4023,66.0,66.6211,67.2656,67.8906,68.5195,69.1484,69.793,70.4414,71.0625,71.7188,72.3477,72.9492,73.5859,74.195